{title: Beyond the River}
{subtitle: Nehemiah 3:7; 3:1–8; 4:1–6; 6:15–16}
{key: Bb}
{tempo: 80}
{time: 6/8}

{comment: Intro}
| [Bb] | [Bb] | [Bb] | [Eb] |
| [Eb] | [Bb] | [Bbmaj7] | [Eb] |
| [Eb] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
Nehemiah [Bb]called the people to the gate
Eliashib and [Gm7]priests began the work
Sheep Gate doors [Eb]were set in their place
The wall rose up for [Fsus4]every single soul
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
Joy of the hand Gisha[Bb]lom repaired the Old Gate
Beams were laid and bolts [Gm7]were made fast
Next to them Melati[Eb]ah of Gibeon stood
And Jadon from Meronot helped [Fsus4]them build
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Men of Gibeon and Mizpah joined [Bb]the line
Under the governor beyond the [Gm7]river
Shoulders to the work, hands on the stone
[Eb]We raised the wall and closed the gap
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
Sanbal[Fsus4]lat and Tobiah were furi[Bb]ous
They conspired to fight against Jerusalem
[Gm7]But we prayed to our God day and night
And post[Eb]ed a guard against their threat
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Men [Fsus4]of Gibeon and Mizpah joined the line
[Bb]Under the governor beyond the river
[Gm7]Shoulders to the work, hands on the stone
We raised [Eb]the wall and closed the gap
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Men of Gibeon [Fsus4]and Mizpah joined the line
Un[Bb]der the governor beyond the river
Shoul[Gm7]ders to the work, hands on the stone
We raised the [Eb]wall and closed the gap
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
The laborers said [Fsus4]the strength was failing
Too much rub[Bb]ble to carry on our backs
But the Jews lived near [Gm7]them and warned us
Turn around and they will [Eb]come and kill
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
Finished in fif-ty-[Fsus4]two days by God
The nations saw and their confidence sank
{end_of_verse}

